Added a `display_prefetch_related` model convention — a list of relation paths that the model's `display`/`__str__` reads — consumed by `BaseTable`, which prefetches them (prefix-joined) whenever a visible column renders that model, whether as the row itself or through a related column. Declared once on a model, it fixes the per-row query in every table anywhere that renders it. Seeded on DeviceType, ModuleType, and Module, replacing the equivalent per-table conditional prefetches.
